{"title":"Career Roadmap · Ayurveda Pharmacist","role":"Ayurveda Pharmacist","summary":"An Ayurveda Pharmacist works with the preparation, processing, quality control, storage, packaging and dispensing of medicines and formulations used within Ayurvedic healthcare systems.","facts":{"Current degree":"Allied Health Sciences (B.Sc / BPT / BOT / BMLT etc.)","Course":"Ayurveda Allied (Panchakarma Technician / Ayurveda Pharmacy)"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"An Ayurveda Pharmacist works with the preparation, processing, quality control, storage, packaging and dispensing of medicines and formulations used within Ayurvedic healthcare systems."},{"type":"p","text":"Depending on qualification, employer and scope of practice, responsibilities may include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Preparation of Ayurvedic formulations"},{"text":"Raw-material identification"},{"text":"Ingredient weighing and processing"},{"text":"Powder, decoction, oil and other formulation preparation"},{"text":"Packaging and labeling"},{"text":"Quality-control support"},{"text":"Inventory management"},{"text":"Storage-condition monitoring"},{"text":"Batch documentation"},{"text":"Pharmacy operations"},{"text":"Supporting Ayurvedic physicians and healthcare facilities"},{"text":"GMP-oriented manufacturing practices"}]},{"type":"note","label":"Important qualification note","text":"“Ayurveda Pharmacist” is a specialized role. A generic B.Sc/BPT/BOT/BMLT qualification should not automatically be treated as an Ayurveda Pharmacy qualification. Students targeting this career should pursue a recognized Ayurveda Pharmacy/related pharmacy qualification accepted by the relevant institution, employer and applicable regulatory framework. Qualification names and eligibility can vary by state, institution and recruitment rules."}]},{"heading":"Career Pathway","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["Class 12","R